<article class="env-lemma" id="02HD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02HD">Lemma <span data-tag="02HD">37.6.6</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume $X$ and $S$ are affine. Then $f$ is formally unramified if and only if $\mathcal{O}_ S(S) \to \mathcal{O}_ X(X)$ is a formally unramified ring map. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is immediate from the definitions (Definition <a href="/tag/02H8" data-tag="02H8">37.6.1</a> and Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/00UN" data-tag="00UN">10.148.1</a>) by the equivalence of categories of rings and affine schemes, see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01I2" data-tag="01I2">26.6.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>